Phase 6 verification report. Scope since the Phase 5 checkpoint e18b398: 15 files - four pure mission modules with tests (missionManager +13, firePacer +11, helperHand +13, sunFx +10), fireFx (+11), helperTrace (+11), a confetti burst added to abilityFx, the HUD's ability/hose visibility, index.html CSS, and main.ts wiring. Automated gates: biome 67 files clean with no warnings, tsc --noEmit clean, CI=true pnpm test 343 tests across 27 files. Coverage is on the logic modules (the FSM, pacer, hand and sun frames are pure and fully exercised); main.ts and src/game/hud are DOM/GLue and excluded by design per workflow.md, which is exactly why this phase's two faults were found by driving frames rather than by tests.

Manual verification, driven through the real frame function after the tab's requestAnimationFrame proved paused while the window was not visible: a fire spawns with a lit flame (scale 1.0 of 4 bursts), cycling smoke, and the ability button hidden; a synthetic pointerdown on the burning house responds, morphs to car-kit/firetruck.glb, and drives over; parking inside HOSE_RANGE gives state active and reveals the hose button; presses take the burst count 4,3,2,1 to 0 and the mission to complete; confetti and the smiling sun fire (sun scale 0.552 on the completing press, 1.015 half a second later, gone by 2 s); the town returns to idle and the ability button comes back; after a fresh fire with no input the hand traced at 9.98 s for 1.8 s and made its demo tap at 11.78 s, leaving the mission active. Console empty throughout.

Two faults found and fixed in this verification, both invisible to the unit tests: the render loop never called mission.update, so a fire could never be reached or doused; and the ability button's visibility was only written on a change so it stayed on screen when a fire started. This is the second phase running where a wiring fault, not a logic fault, was the thing the verification caught, after Phase 5's burst clock. Caveat recorded honestly: screenshots were unavailable (the browser tab was not visible on the desktop), so the flame, smoke, confetti and sun were confirmed programmatically rather than by eye, and a human playtest of the full mission on the tablet remains part of Phase 8.
